<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Compound amount and interest</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} invests Ksh \({@ksh(P)@}\) at \({@dd(r)@}\%\) per annum compound interest, added at the end of each year.</p><p>(a) Find the amount after \({@n@}\) years, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the compound interest earned.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>With compound interest, interest is added to the account, and next year's interest is paid on the bigger sum. Each year the amount is multiplied by \(1 + \frac{ {@dd(r)@} }{100} = {@dd(mult)@}\).</p><p>(a) \(A = P\left(1 + \dfrac{r}{100}\right)^n = {@ksh(P)@} \times {@dd(mult)@}^{ {@n@} } = {@ksh(A)@}\), so the amount is Ksh \({@ksh(floor(A+1/2))@}\) to the nearest shilling. Round only at the end.</p><p>(b) Compound interest \(= A - P = {@ksh(A)@} - {@ksh(P)@} = {@ksh(CI)@}\)[[if test="not(integerp(CI))"]], about Ksh \({@ksh(floor(CI+1/2))@}\)[[/if]].</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: A = P(1 + r/100)^n in Kenyan contexts. [P, r, n]. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), chapter 5, section 3.1, and SMP GCSE Higher book 1, chapter 8, C2 and C3. */
L: [[35000,9,3],[125000,15/2,4],[8500,12,2],[72000,21/2,3],[250000,13/2,5],[18600,11,4],[46000,8,5],[95000,13,2],[15600,19/2,3],[320000,7,4]];
E: L[ix];
P: E[1]; r: E[2]; n: E[3];
nm: ["Achieng","Kiprono","Wanjiru","Omondi","Nekesa","Mutua","Chebet","Barasa","Njeri","Hassan"][ix];
mult: 1+r/100;
A: P*mult^n;
CI: A-P;
/* diagnostics */
As: P*(1+r*n/100);
Am: P*mult^(n-1);
Ap: P*mult^(n+1);
SI: P*r*n/100;
Y1: P*r/100;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
