  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Commercial Arithmetic III: compound amount and interest</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.4 (b): Find the amount and the compound interest on a savings deposit, with interest added once a year, using A = P(1 + r/100)^n.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5 (Practical arithmetic), Section 3.1 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: growth of a fixed sum by the same percentage each year, with the year-by-year approach of SMP GCSE Higher 1, Chapter 8, Section C; Kenyan contexts and new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
